1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,629
BRAMBLE: Case open!

2
00:00:01,629 --> 00:00:05,831
OTTO: Hey! That's not fair! Ivy didn't count!

3
00:00:06,031 --> 00:00:09,728
IVY: I didn't need to. I just saw it.

4
00:00:10,028 --> 00:00:13,866
Today's case: ladybird dots at a glance.

5
00:00:14,166 --> 00:00:17,577
At a glance means one quick look.

6
00:00:17,877 --> 00:00:21,023
Like the dots on a dice.

7
00:00:21,623 --> 00:00:25,135
Mabel painted this ladybird stepping stone.

8
00:00:25,335 --> 00:00:28,428
How many dots does it have?

9
00:00:28,828 --> 00:00:34,410
OTTO: I'll count. One, two, three, four, five!

10
00:00:34,610 --> 00:00:37,905
IVY: Hmm. I saw four at a glance.

11
00:00:38,105 --> 00:00:40,173
OTTO: Four? You guessed!

12
00:00:40,573 --> 00:00:43,517
BRAMBLE: Let's not guess. Let's test.

13
00:00:43,917 --> 00:00:46,642
BRAMBLE: Can you point to the dots?

14
00:00:49,742 --> 00:00:53,265
BRAMBLE: How many dots? Take a quick look.

15
00:00:53,665 --> 00:00:55,988
A. Five dots.

16
00:00:56,188 --> 00:00:59,103
B. Four dots.

17
00:00:59,303 --> 00:01:01,328
Pause and think.

18
00:01:05,928 --> 00:01:09,415
You can see small groups without counting.

19
00:01:10,015 --> 00:01:12,757
Two dots on this wing.

20
00:01:13,157 --> 00:01:15,829
Two dots on that wing.

21
00:01:16,229 --> 00:01:19,168
Two and two make four.

22
00:01:19,768 --> 00:01:21,912
It's B! Four dots.

23
00:01:22,112 --> 00:01:25,289
OTTO: Oh! I touched one dot twice!

24
00:01:25,689 --> 00:01:27,940
BRAMBLE: Let's check another way.

25
00:01:28,140 --> 00:01:30,854
Touch each dot only once.

26
00:01:31,054 --> 00:01:34,949
One, two, three, four.

27
00:01:35,349 --> 00:01:38,265
IVY: Four! Same as my quick look!

28
00:01:38,665 --> 00:01:39,979
BRAMBLE: Case solved!

29
00:01:41,479 --> 00:01:44,504
OTTO: Hello, tiny ladybird! Can you count?

30
00:01:44,704 --> 00:01:46,850
IVY: Ladybirds can't count, Otto!

31
00:01:47,250 --> 00:01:51,401
Remember. You can see small groups without counting.

32
00:01:51,901 --> 00:01:58,055
Say it with me. You can see small groups without counting.

33
00:01:59,855 --> 00:02:05,201
Try it at home. Roll a dice. Say the number fast!

34
00:02:05,701 --> 00:02:08,773
Next case: the shuffled clue cards.

